# The build context, narrowed.
#
# The Dockerfile COPYs four directories by name, so nothing else can reach the
# image — but everything not excluded here is still SENT to the daemon on every
# build, and this repository's largest directories are the ones no plane needs.
#
# 🛑 AN EXCLUSION HERE OUTRANKS A `COPY` THERE, AND IT DOES NOT LOSE QUIETLY.
# A path excluded from the context never reaches the daemon, so a `COPY` naming
# it does not silently copy nothing — the build FAILS, before any of the layers
# below it, and both planes die with it. This file listed `model` while the
# Dockerfile had already gained `COPY model ./model`; the two disagreed and the
# image could not be built at all. `tests/http/engine-on-served-path.test.ts`
# now subtracts this file's exclusions from that file's `COPY` set, so the pair
# cannot disagree again without an assertion saying so.
#
# ⚠️ `node_modules` FIRST AND FOR A REASON BEYOND SPEED. `npm ci --omit=dev` runs
# inside the image; a host `node_modules` copied in would be the DEVELOPMENT tree,
# built against a different platform, and it would shadow the install. That
# failure looks like a native-binding error at start-up and reads like a bug in
# the driver.
node_modules
.git
.github

# Not a plane's business.
#
# ⚠️ `model` WAS IN THIS LIST AND IS DELIBERATELY GONE. It is removed rather than
# negated with `!model` so that this list holds one rule per line and no line
# argues with another. The reason it was here is still the right reason for the
# names that remain — a plane has no business with a test, a checker or a
# mockup — and it stopped being true of `model/` the moment
# `server/data-plane/run-vocabulary.ts` made `RUN_TRIGGER_KINDS` a VALUE import
# on the served path. See the `COPY model ./model` comment in `Dockerfile`.
tests
tools
Mockups
assets
design
.claude
.impeccable

# `docs/contracts/` IS copied in — ruling 1 makes it the router, not documentation.
# Everything else under docs/ is the design record and does not ship.
docs/*
!docs/contracts

*.md
compose.yaml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
